## [:< ##

# name  = plugin.user-edit.key-details.tab_info
# descr = key-details plugin's self-description
# param = -none-

## read-only 'key details' tab : the invoking Unix user's own C25519 identity
## [ name / checksum / public key ], shown only on their OWN record -- see
## plugin.user-edit.key-details.render's header.
##
## NO pinned_keys, deliberately : pinning is for fields that exist in the
## record's own $fields hash [ plugin.user-edit.registry.post_init's by_key
## lookup, consulted by form.schema_from_record's per-field loop and
## form.handler.stdin_key's Right-entry trigger ].  this plugin's one field is
## SYNTHESISED in schema_from_record instead [ key/identity data is not record
## data ], already carrying plugin =>  'plugin.user-edit.key-details' on its
## own field_def -- and keeping 'identity_key' OUT of by_key is exactly what
## keeps stdin_key's plugin-mode entry trigger from ever firing on it.  this
## tab_info exists for the registry's bookkeeping/discovery only.
## registry.post_init tolerates a missing pinned_keys [ '( ... // [] )' ], so
## no registry change was needed for this shape.
##
## q|..|, NOT qw|..| : qw splits on WHITESPACE, so qw| key details | would
## collapse into label => 'key' plus a stray 'details' key -- the same trap
## plugin.user-edit.example.render's own header documents for format strings,
## applied here to the label itself
return { qw| label | => q| key details |, };

